धम् (ध्मा), ध॑मति (˚ते), pp. धमित॑ & ध्मात॑
blow, exhale;
 kindle (fire by blowing), melt (ore). — अनु blow upon.
अप blow off. अभि blow at, terrify by blowing. आ inflate, blow,
sound, proclaim aloud;
 P. be inflated or puffed up. उपा & समुपा
blow, sound. उद् exhale, breathe out, proclaim. उप blow at (acc.).
निस् & परा blow away. प्र blow forth, blow away i.e. terrify by
blowing, blow at (acc.);
 M. proclaim aloud. C. blow into (a conchshell),
sound. वि blow i.e. drive asunder, scatter, disperse, destroy. सम्
blow or melt together;
 proclaim aloud.

धमन a. blowing away, scaring (—˚);
 n. the melting (of
ore).

धम॑नि f. piping;
 reed, pipe;
 tube or canal of the human
body, vessel, vein, nerve, etc.

धा॑मन् n. seat, home, residence, realm (of the gods);
 wont
or favourite place, thing, or person;
 inmates, family, troop, host (also
pl.);
 law, rule;
 custom, rite, manner;
 strength, power, majesty,
splendour (also pl.);
 N. of a Ṛṣi.
